<Base title="About" description="Why IntoTheTwilightZone.com exists, how it is built, and how to contact the site.">
  <h1>About IntoTheTwilightZone.com</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    IntoTheTwilightZone.com is a fan-curated, non-commercial reference to The Twilight Zone: every series,
    episode and person, and the long trail of films, songs, books and stories the show inspired.
  </p>
  <p>
    It began with a kid watching the New Year's Twilight Zone marathons on television, and grew into years of
    notes, spreadsheets and research. The goal is simple: document the franchise carefully, cite where every fact
    comes from, and share it freely. The site carries no advertising, sells nothing and earns no money.
  </p>
  <h2>How entries work</h2>
  <p>
    Every episode, film, song and book is a record with its sources attached. Links between works, such as a film
    inspired by an episode, are labelled by how well they are documented: confirmed by the creator, documented by a
    reliable source, or fan-noted and still awaiting a source. Read the full <a href="/sources/">sourcing policy</a>.
  </p>
  <h2 id="disclaimer">Disclaimer</h2>
  <p>
    This is an independent fan site. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by CBS Studios, Paramount,
    the Rod Serling estate, or any rights holder. The Twilight Zone is a trademark of CBS Studios Inc. All other
    trademarks and copyrighted works belong to their respective owners and are referenced for commentary, criticism
    and historical documentation.
  </p>
  <h2 id="privacy">Privacy</h2>
  <p>Reading the site sets no cookies, and the site runs no advertising and no tracking scripts. Member accounts use only the cookies needed to keep you signed in. The <a href="/privacy/">privacy notice</a> explains exactly what an account stores and how to download or delete it.</p>
  <h2 id="contact">Contact and corrections</h2>
  <p>
    Found an error, have a source for a fan-noted connection, or represent a rights holder with a concern? Please
    <a href="https://github.com/fortechsupport/intothetwilightzone/issues/new" rel="noopener">open an issue on GitHub</a>.
    Rights-holder requests are handled promptly, and content is removed or corrected while a request is reviewed.
  </p>
</Base>
